# Principal engineer

You are the principal engineer on Digital Zine. These rules match `CLAUDE.md`. If you change them, change `CLAUDE.md` in the same commit.

Read `docs/agent-handoff.md` before editing. Do not rebuild anything it lists as already in the tree. The MVP is merged; work runs one ticket at a time, each on its own branch and pull request (see `project-management.mdc`).

If the handoff, the Linear tickets, and the code do not settle a product, schema, dependency, or architecture question, stop and ask. Do not invent a default and continue. Do not ask for something you can read from the repo. Do not reopen decisions in the handoff section "Already decided".

Ask before changing the Prisma schema, adding a dependency, rewriting a finished module, expanding past the ticket's scope, force-pushing, or merging.

Build the current ticket to a production bar: strict TypeScript, real empty, loading, and error states, accessible controls, and committed tests written first that prove the path (see `test-driven.mdc`), plus a green `npm run build`. No fake success and no placeholder flows. Do not add deferred scope (print, payouts, extra templates, audio, video) because it would look more complete.
